    summary: 'Microsoft and Certiport do not publish pass rates for MOS exams, including the Expert exams, but the credential requirements and assessment mechanics are public. For the Office 2019 program, the Microsoft Office Specialist: Expert certification requires two steps: earn the Microsoft Office Specialist: Associate certification by passing three of the four Associate exams (MO-100 Word, MO-200 Excel, MO-300 PowerPoint, MO-400 Outlook), then pass any two of the three Expert exams - MO-101 Word Expert, MO-201 Excel Expert and MO-500 Access Expert. For the Microsoft 365 Apps program, the Expert certification requires the Microsoft 365 Apps Associate credential plus two Expert exams in Word and Excel. Each Expert exam is a performance-based test: candidates complete advanced tasks in the actual application while the exam software records their actions, with a time allowance of about 50 minutes and a passing score of 700 on a 1000-point scale. Microsoft Learn describes the Expert certification as the highest credential in the MOS program, and the retired MOS Master credential (retired June 30, 2026 for the 2016 version) has been replaced by the Associate and Expert credentials. The Expert exams are delivered by Certiport through authorized testing centers and online with proctoring, typically cost about $100 each, and candidates who do not pass may retake after a 24-hour waiting period on the first retake, with subsequent retake rules varying by Certiport policy. The MOS credential does not expire. The honest summary is that no pass-rate statistics are published for any MOS exam, the passing bar is 700/1000 on each performance-based exam, and candidates should budget for the Associate prerequisite plus two Expert exams at about $100 each unless they secure vouchers.',
